<h2 id="ha-ctrl-004-acceptance">Acceptance and evidence</h2>

1. Test an on and off only light, a brightness-only light, tunable white, colour and a light running an effect. Unsupported controls must not appear.
2. Test an off light with a remembered colour, an unavailable member and a mixed room. Check the list of lights the action will affect and the result for each member.
3. Change all ten interface palettes and both tones. No light command or device colour conversion may happen.
4. Use keyboard colour controls, precise text values, a 320px layout, the native locale and a failed request. Check capabilities again after a firmware or integration change.

Record the Home Assistant and frontend versions, browser, fixture or device, input state, expected result, observed result and where the evidence is kept. Reviewing the source or this page is not a test on a connected device.

For the native definitions, see the Home Assistant documentation for [Light](https://www.home-assistant.io/integrations/light/), [light entity capabilities](https://contributors.home-assistant.io/core/entities/light/) and [card features](https://www.home-assistant.io/dashboards/features/).
